It is Sunday evening.
Asha rings my doorbell.
Moti hears it and runs towards the door.
He wags his tail quickly.
I open the door.
Asha comes inside and asks, 'How is my Moti?'
Moti jumps on her.
I laugh and say, 'He was a good guest.'
I give Moti's bowl and leash to Asha.
I say, 'Please take these.'
Asha asks, 'Did he eat his food on time?'
I say, 'Yes, I looked after him well.'
'But there is a small problem.'
I bring my sandal.
There are teeth marks on the shoe.
'He chewed my shoe!'
'I told him that this must not be eaten.'
Asha looks at the shoe and laughs loudly.
She says, 'Oh Moti!'
'You must not do this!'
I say, 'Do not worry, this is an old shoe.'
Asha says, 'Thank you, Maya.'
She leads him and goes to her home.
